body:
### Description

I'm trying to use `@ai-sdk/google-vertex` alongside Cloudflare's AI Gateway, 

The following works as-intended with Google's Generative AI provider:

```typescript
export const googleGenerativeAiSdk = createGoogleGenerativeAI({
  apiKey: GCP_API_KEY,
  baseURL: `${CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL}/google-ai-studio/v1beta`,
  headers: {
    "cf-aig-authorization": `Bearer ${CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN}`,
  },
});
```

However the same logic fails when using Vertex AI alongside Google's Vertex AI.

```typescript
export const vertexAiSdk = createVertex({
  baseURL:
    CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL +
    `/google-vertex-ai/v1/projects/${GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY.project_id}/locations/${GCP_REGION}/publishers/google`,
  googleAuthOptions: {
    credentials: GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY,
  },
  project: GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY.project_id,
  location: GCP_REGION,
  headers: {
    "cf-aig-authorization": `Bearer ${CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN}`,
  },
});
```
Which results in 
> APICallError [AI_APICallError]: Request is missing required authentication credential. Expected OAuth 2 access token, login cookie or other valid authentication credential. See https://developers.google.com/identity/sign-in/web/devconsole-project.



### Code example

_No response_

### AI provider

@ai-sdk/google v1.1.16

### Additional context

Through testing, I've discovered that if I remove the `headers` object from the `createVertex` then the request succeeds, however I am forced to disable authentication for my Cloudflare Gateway. 

If I try to manually generate the ID token and provide it in the headers object, the request succeeds.

```typescript
 headers: async () => ({
    authorization: "Bearer " + (await GoogleAuthClient.getAccessToken()),
    "cf-aig-authorization": `Bearer ${CLOUDFLARE_AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN}`,
  });
```

I still believe this to be a bug, however, because the behavior works correctly in one library and not in the other, and it doesn't make sense for `@ai-sdk/google-vertex` to collect authorization credentials from me while still requiring me to generate my own ID token in the header.
